+# Diegetic UI (UI in the world)
+
+## Setting one up
+Diegetic Screen Actor (Place Actors, or Add > Diegetic Screen on any actor as a component): pick its Widget Class - any Widget Blueprint, built as for the HUD. Sizing Physical Size: the screen's width and height in cm, Pixel Density pixels per cm (12 = a 160 x 90 cm screen at 1920 x 1080; 8-12 reads well from a step away). Every local player's pawn gets a Diegetic Interactor on its own (Project Settings > Plugins > Diegetic UI), aiming from the camera's centre: look at a button and click (left mouse, gamepad left face button). Nothing else to set up.
+
+## Cost
+Update Mode: By Distance (default: every frame within Near Distance, Mid Rate, Far Rate per second beyond), When Changed (redraws only while an animation plays, the player points at it, or Mark Diegetic Content Changed is called - for signs and menus), Every Frame (a hero screen). Max Update Distance keeps the last frame beyond; Cull Distance hides it. A per-frame budget (Max Redraws Per Frame, 6) spreads redraws over frames. Screens pointed at redraw every frame. The widget ticks when its screen redraws. Console: stat NameTBDDiegetic, NameTBD.Diegetic.Debug 1.
+
+## Presence and use
+Wake Distance (0 = always awake): the widget's Anim In plays as the player comes near, Anim Out as they leave; While Asleep freezes, hides or keeps updating. Use Mode Point And Click, or Focus View: a click moves the camera in front of the screen, the cursor shows (or the D-pad moves focus, A presses), Escape / B leaves - a terminal or computer. Use Not Usable for signs.
+
+## The widget hears the screen
+State machine inputs set on the widget's own state machines when they have them: ScreenAwake, ScreenAimedAt, ScreenInUse (Bool), ScreenDistance (Number, cm) - light a screen up as the player looks at it with no Blueprint. Or implement the Diegetic Screen Widget interface (On Screen Wake / Sleep / Aim Changed / Use Changed / Back). Pointer Position, Hover/Press and Drag value inputs read the world pointer on a screen, so card tilts and hover glows work in the world. UI sounds (buttons, cards, Sound cues) play from the widget's place on the screen (Sound > Play Sounds In The World).
+
+## Look
+Create Screen Material (the screen's Details) makes a glowing screen material; Screen Look sets Brightness (above 1 blooms), scan lines, CRT curvature, colour fringing, vignette, flicker and grain.
+
+## Not yet
+Info Cards from an anchor on a screen still open on the HUD (only To Viewport placement is right there).
